Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:14:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] xpia-steering integration: plugin target-LLM seam,
 reachability override, Azure optimizer provider + call cache

- get_llm: 'plugin:<module>?k=v' resolves to module.make_llm(spec) -> BasePipelineElement
  (defense-inside-the-LLM targets, e.g. activation steering, which the register_defense
  filter seam cannot express)
- optimize_variants: plugin specs require --target-model-id for the cache path;
  AUTODOJO_REACHABILITY_LLM builds the reachability pipeline from a second (undefended)
  spec, per the evaluator's own reachability-must-be-undefended design
- llm_utils: provider 'azure' (XPIA_JUDGE_ENDPOINT + az-cli AAD bearer, 40-min refresh,
  gpt-5*: max_completion_tokens + temperature omitted), usage into cost_tracker,
  occurrence-indexed on-disk call cache (AUTODOJO_LLM_CACHE)

Upstream pinned at abbcbd8d59ea19115dc874eeb2cf294169ac5e0d.
